---
source: crates/ostro/tests/cli_p11.rs
expression: "help(&[\"bulk\", \"rerun\"])"
---
Rerun the selected runs from a cut

Usage: ostro bulk rerun [OPTIONS] <--from-step <NAME[#N]>|--from-seq <N>>

Options:
      --from-step <NAME[#N]>       Cut before the N-th (1-based, default 1) execution of step NAME: `NAME` or `NAME#N`
      --from-seq <N>               Cut at journal sequence number N (events before N are copied)
      --version <active|source|N>  Version to execute: `active` (server default), `source` or a number
      --tag <TAGS>                 Tag filter (repeatable; every tag must match)
      --status <STATUS>            Status filter [possible values: scheduled, ready, running, completed, failed, cancelled, terminated, timed_out, continued_as_new]
      --workflow <WORKFLOW>        Workflow filter
      --queue <QUEUE>              Queue filter
      --dlq                        Only DLQ members
      --rate <N>                   Operations per second (server default `[bulk] default_rate`, capped at `max_rate`)
      --max-in-flight <N>          Concurrent operations (server default `[bulk] max_in_flight`)
      --dry-run                    Count and sample the matches only; create no job
      --server <SERVER>            Server URL [env: OSTRO_SERVER=] [default: http://127.0.0.1:7700]
      --json                       Print the REST response body as JSON
      --timeout <TIMEOUT>          Per-request timeout (friendly duration; a long-poll adds its wait) [default: 30s]
      --ca-file <PEM>              PEM CA certificate to trust for an https:// server instead of the platform roots (e.g. the cluster CA `<data_dir>/tls/ca.crt` behind a self-signed listener) [env: OSTRO_CA_FILE=]
  -h, --help                       Print help
